 "summary": "The new kernel/cokernel exponent-independence results for `D\u2080 + \u03b1` and the planar strong-solution regularity theorem have no existing counterpart in Mathlib or TauCeti, and they are built from existing lemmas (`memWkpLoc_one_of_le`, `isWeakCRSolution_iff_ae`, `kerEquivOfRegularity`, `cokerEquivOfRegularity`, `isFredholm_perturbedSobolevL`). The smooth analogue in `CauchyRiemann/Exponent.lean` uses a different argument that does not cover `\u03b1 \u2208 L\u1d56`, so this is not a duplicate.",
